From 4f6572fcd500f4853f5f876aa92610421d541e24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: salvamalfa <salvamalfas@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:26:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/19] Reserve env slots for the estimator's seed source

OpenSky is free for non-commercial use and can supply flights per carrier
per route per month, which is the one input the route-carrier estimator
still lacks. Registration sits behind a CAPTCHA, so the account is created
by hand and only the resulting credentials are wired here.

Both shapes are reserved: the OAuth2 client pair the current API expects,
and username/password as a fallback if the account page offers no API
client. No credentials are committed; .env stays gitignored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYLfAv93wjCxnGdihXYpAm
---
 .env.example | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.env.example b/.env.example
index ece923b..eadab51 100644
--- a/.env.example
+++ b/.env.example
@@ -8,3 +8,14 @@ BANXICO_TOKEN=""
 # Optional. FRED can be used instead of EIA where an equivalent series exists.
 EIA_API_KEY=""
 FRED_API_KEY=""
+
+# Optional. Seed source for the route-carrier estimator (flights per carrier per
+# route per month). Free for non-commercial use; the account has to be created
+# by hand because registration is behind a CAPTCHA.
+# Create the account at opensky-network.org, then generate an API client from
+# the account page and paste the pair here.
+OPENSKY_CLIENT_ID=""
+OPENSKY_CLIENT_SECRET=""
+# Fallback if the account page offers no API client and only basic auth works.
+OPENSKY_USERNAME=""
+OPENSKY_PASSWORD=""
